-- Buffer state machine: push/pop items, buffer never goes negative.
--
-- A bounded buffer processes events that either push an item onto the
-- buffer or pop an item from it. The state.pop atom has
-- requires: Le(0, input) and guarantee: LengthSubOne(output, input) ∧ Le(0, output),
-- so the fixpoint discovers length-related invariants and Le(0, buffer).
--
-- Invariant: length-related predicates + Le(0, buffer) -- INFERRED.
-- Termination: Constant (side-channel; event stream passes through).

rec { (arr("state.push") ||| arr("state.pop")) >>> first(id) }
